 "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (multiple indoor units, H-Link)",
 "applies_to": "Hitachi and Hisense VRF systems on the H-Link (TB2) bus.",
 "summary": "Intesis 700 Series multi-protocol gateway set up for BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP on a Hitachi or Hisense H-Link bus. It publishes gateway-wide commands, a block of outdoor-unit objects at (OU address x 25) + 20000 and a block of indoor-unit objects at (IU address x 100): on/off, mode, setpoint, fan, louver, coil and air temperatures, error code, filter, remote-controller permissions, dehumidification and energy consumption.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Indoor unit instance = (IU address x 100) + offset; IU address 1 is shown (100-120). Outdoor unit instance = (OU address x 25) + 20000 + offset; OU address 0 is shown (20000-20006).",
  "The Hitachi and Hisense manuals (both v1.1.8, 2025-12-09) print the same BACnet object table; this one entry covers both.",
  "With an SPX-RAMHLK adapter only part of the objects is supported (marked in the Hitachi manual).",
  "The BACnet table has no read/write column; access is inferred from object type (outputs commandable, inputs read-only).",
  "Consumption objects report Wh or kWh as set in Intesis MAPS.",
  "Replaces the older INBACHIT016O000/064O000 BACnet server (listed separately), which used different outdoor-unit instances."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "700 Series Air Gateway IN770AIR***O000 - Hitachi VRF Systems to Modbus, KNX, BACnet, MQTT and Home Automation - User Manual",
